{"name":"Scallywag","hex":"#e5d5bd","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"scallywag","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A disreputable fellow, a good-for-nothing, a scapegrace, a blackguard","A badly behaved person, especially a child; a mischief-maker; a rascal"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scallywag"}],"entries":[{"title":"Scallywag (magazine)","blocks":[{"text":"Scallywag magazine was published in London between 1991 and 1995. The subtitle of issues 1 - 6 was \"Camden's only alternative community magazine\". It sought to publish controversial journalism which other satirical and investigative publications were said to be unwilling to publish over fears of litigation. It was founded and edited by Simon Regan and Angus James, Regan's half-brother."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scallywag_(magazine)"},{"title":"Auxiliary Units","blocks":[{"text":"The Auxiliary Units, Home Guard Shock Squads or GHQ Auxiliary Units were specially trained, highly secret quasi military units created by the British government during the Second World War with the aim of using irregular warfare in response to a possible invasion of the United Kingdom by Nazi Germany. With the advantage of having witnessed the rapid fall of several Continental European nations, the United Kingdom was the only country during the war that was able to create a guerrilla force in anticipation of an invasion."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auxiliary_Units"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Parham_airfield%2C_Museum_of_the_British_Resistance_Organisation_-_Auxiliary_unit_operational_base.jpg/500px-Parham_airfield%2C_Museum_of_the_British_Resistance_Organisation_-_Auxiliary_unit_operational_base.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Parham_airfield%2C_Museum_of_the_British_Resistance_Organisation_-_Auxiliary_unit_operational_base.jpg/1280px-Parham_airfield%2C_Museum_of_the_British_Resistance_Organisation_-_Auxiliary_unit_operational_base.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Parham_airfield%2C_Museum_of_the_British_Resistance_Organisation_-_Auxiliary_unit_operational_base.jpg/500px-Parham_airfield%2C_Museum_of_the_British_Resistance_Organisation_-_Auxiliary_unit_operational_base.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Operational Base reconstruction at Parham Airfield Museum, Suffolk","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AParham_airfield%2C_Museum_of_the_British_Resistance_Organisation_-_Auxiliary_unit_operational_base.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Auxiliary_Units%2C_Operational_Base%2C_emergency_exit%2C_Wivelsfield.png/500px-Auxiliary_Units%2C_Operational_Base%2C_emergency_exit%2C_Wivelsfield.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Auxiliary_Units%2C_Operational_Base%2C_emergency_exit%2C_Wivelsfield.png/1280px-Auxiliary_Units%2C_Operational_Base%2C_emergency_exit%2C_Wivelsfield.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Auxiliary_Units%2C_Operational_Base%2C_emergency_exit%2C_Wivelsfield.png/500px-Auxiliary_Units%2C_Operational_Base%2C_emergency_exit%2C_Wivelsfield.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Auxiliary Units, Operational Base, emergency exit","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAuxiliary_Units%2C_Operational_Base%2C_emergency_exit%2C_Wivelsfield.png"}],"sounds":{"scallywag":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/09/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-scallywag.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.o